# module Shared turn runtime

Owns the shape-neutral primitives used by both extracted HTTP handlers: caller-tool
sink buffering and park races, MCP bench URL construction, dead-session watching,
per-turn usage/cost settlement, continuation transcript remembering, timeout error
construction, and stop-reason mapping. Handler modules import these exports;
`server.js` only composes and routes.

# invariant One state machine

Chat and Responses may shape different response objects, but they share exactly one
implementation of pending-turn buffering, usage baseline advancement, dead-session
retirement and tool-call race ordering. Do not copy these primitives back into a
handler or introduce a universal DI container.
